WEBVTT

00:00:01.491 --> 00:00:03.408
[PHOENIX] The Kurain Village's
sacred urn was stolen

00:00:03.491 --> 00:00:06.950
by the infamous phantom
thief "Mask DeMasque."

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.075
Shortly thereafter,
a man named Ron DeLite

00:00:09.158 --> 00:00:11.991
surrendered, claiming to be
the man behind the mask.

00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:14.450
But something about his
claim didn't sit right with me,

00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:16.200
and I took up his case.

00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:18.366
At the trial,
I was able to prove that Ron

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.825
didn't steal the urn,
and even unmasked

00:00:20.908 --> 00:00:22.950
the true DeMasque
in the process.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.116
The culprit was his
rival, Ace Detective Luke Atmey.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.033
We won the case,
but then Ron was accused

00:00:28.116 --> 00:00:30.033
of something far worse.

00:02:06.241 --> 00:02:07.200
[PHOENIX sighs]

00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:09.491
I'm glad we got
the urn back, but...

00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:11.450
[PHOENIX] To do it, we had
to place Ron at the scene

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:13.575
of a murder as it happened.

00:02:13.658 --> 00:02:14.825
I just don't buy it.

00:02:14.908 --> 00:02:16.991
How could that wimp
commit murder?

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:18.950
Well. What else
could he have been doing?

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.616
Mr. Nick proved he
was there at 1 AM.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.116
Establishing an alibi's
a really strong move.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.116
As long as it's verifiable, it
can turn an entire case around.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.533
I was just trying
to prove Ron was

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.950
somewhere else at the time.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.950
[MAYA] Too bad that
"somewhere else" was where

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.491
a murder took place.

00:02:34.575 --> 00:02:37.033
Looks like you did
too good of a job this time.

00:02:37.116 --> 00:02:38.408
What can I say?

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.366
I didn't know they'd
find a body there.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.116
I'm worried.
I hope Desirée's okay.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.783
This can't be easy on her.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.450
All right.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:50.533
We should investigate the
murder at K-B Security.

00:02:50.616 --> 00:02:52.908
I don't think Ron has it in
him to kill someone, either.

00:02:52.991 --> 00:02:54.866
There must be
another explanation.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.658
I'll continue to defend him.

00:02:56.741 --> 00:02:58.283
For his wife's sake, too.

00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:00.075
--[MAYA] Good call.
--[PEARL] And with the urn back,

00:03:00.158 --> 00:03:02.741
we can focus our efforts
on helping you.

00:03:02.825 --> 00:03:04.908
Oh. Yeah, that reminds me.

00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:07.533
Did the urn always
have these pink splotches?

00:03:07.616 --> 00:03:11.283
And what's with it saying
"AMI" again all of a sudden?

00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:14.366
It still said "I AM"
on the poster.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.033
[PHOENIX]
The truth is, one year ago,

00:03:16.116 --> 00:03:18.033
Pearl broke the urn by accident.

00:03:18.116 --> 00:03:20.158
She tried her best to
put it back together,

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:24.116
but she isn't exactly great
at crafts... or spelling.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.783
Whoa! I just had a thought.

00:03:25.866 --> 00:03:28.033
Do you think this could
be a fake or something?

00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:29.741
[PHOENIX]
A-A fake?

00:03:29.825 --> 00:03:31.700
If you really think so,
then I'll bring it back to

00:03:31.783 --> 00:03:34.491
the village and have
Great Aunt take a look at it!

00:03:34.575 --> 00:03:36.075
[MAYA]
Good idea! I'll go with you.

00:03:36.158 --> 00:03:38.950
Oh, no. I couldn't
possibly allow that.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.158
[MAYA]
Why not?

00:03:40.241 --> 00:03:42.575
I want you two to spend
some time together.

00:03:42.658 --> 00:03:44.158
Maybe then you'll
get all lovey-dovey

00:03:44.241 --> 00:03:45.533
like our new friends are.

00:03:45.616 --> 00:03:46.908
"Like our new friends?"

00:03:46.991 --> 00:03:50.075
[PEARL] You know! I mean
Ron and Desirée, obviously!

00:03:50.158 --> 00:03:51.616
Taking matters
into their own hands

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.283
to defend each other.
Oh! So romantic!

00:03:55.366 --> 00:03:57.075
Now that's what I call love!

00:03:57.158 --> 00:03:58.908
I hope I feel that one day!

00:03:58.991 --> 00:04:00.200
Someone's excited.

00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:01.658
You can say that again.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.325
[PEARL] I'm off!
Be a good couple while I'm gone.

00:04:04.408 --> 00:04:05.825
No fighting, okay?

00:04:07.158 --> 00:04:08.491
She, uh...

00:04:08.575 --> 00:04:11.325
Seems to have the wrong
impression about the two of us.

00:04:11.408 --> 00:04:14.700
I know. Right?
I'm not surprised though.

00:04:14.783 --> 00:04:15.783
Why's that?

00:04:15.866 --> 00:04:18.033
I'm sure I've
told you this before.

00:04:18.116 --> 00:04:20.616
But our channeling powers
are strictly maternal.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.658
Only the women inherit them.

00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:25.283
So inevitably,
we become the center of life

00:04:25.366 --> 00:04:27.866
in the village.
Maybe because of that,

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.158
many marriages in our
family end up falling apart.

00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:33.616
I guess the men
must feel like outsiders.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.783
Because many of them end up
leaving the village forever.

00:04:36.866 --> 00:04:38.450
Even when they have a daughter.

00:04:38.533 --> 00:04:41.658
I take it Pearls's father wasn't
the exception, then.

00:04:41.741 --> 00:04:42.825
It's just...

00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:44.491
She's grown up surrounded
by relationships

00:04:44.575 --> 00:04:46.450
that never seem
to work out well.

00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:49.533
It's only natural she'd want
to encourage healthy ones.

00:04:49.616 --> 00:04:51.575
Besides, ever since
the incident last year,

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.533
she hasn't had a mom around.

00:04:53.616 --> 00:04:55.366
Oh. Yeah.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.741
[PHOENIX]
That's right.

00:04:56.825 --> 00:04:58.908
Pearls's mother, Morgan Fey,
has been rotting in jail

00:04:58.991 --> 00:05:01.825
for the last year.

00:05:01.908 --> 00:05:03.366
So I get it.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:06.075
I mean, I'm the only family
she's got left at this point.

00:05:06.158 --> 00:05:07.533
That makes a lot of sense.

00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:08.991
[ANDREWS]
Um, excuse me.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:12.908
[PHOENIX gasps]
Ms. Andrews? What's the matter?

00:05:12.991 --> 00:05:17.075
I... have some bad news.
I'm truly sorry!

00:05:17.158 --> 00:05:18.575
[BOTH gasps]

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:27.575
Really? You shattered
the Kurain urn?

00:05:27.658 --> 00:05:28.616
Yes.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.616
[MAYA]
But... When did that happen?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.825
Recently. It was
about two weeks ago.

00:05:33.908 --> 00:05:35.700
The urn was sent
to us after they finished

00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:37.783
the photo shoot for the poster.

00:05:37.866 --> 00:05:40.241
I was carrying it to the
warehouse when it happened.

00:05:40.325 --> 00:05:42.283
[ANDREWS wails]

00:05:45.325 --> 00:05:46.325
[gasps]

00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:49.450
[screams]

00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:50.950
[shattering]

00:05:53.283 --> 00:05:55.783
[screams]

00:05:55.866 --> 00:05:58.408
[ANDREWS] I'll never forget
that terrible noise.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.033
I rushed over and
tried to check inside.

00:06:01.908 --> 00:06:03.325
[screams]

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:09.283
[whimpers, sighs]

00:06:10.491 --> 00:06:12.283
[ANDREWS] And then
blacked out from the shock.

00:06:14.283 --> 00:06:15.866
[MAYA]
Yeah, that checks out.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:18.033
The paint matches perfectly.

00:06:18.116 --> 00:06:21.575
Of course... I tried
my best to repair the urn.

00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:23.241
Fortunately, the shards
were pretty big,

00:06:23.325 --> 00:06:27.700
so I was able to piece them back
together with relative ease.

00:06:27.783 --> 00:06:28.991
With the urn
back in one piece,

00:06:29.075 --> 00:06:31.908
I realized how ugly the
paint stains looked.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.366
So I hid them behind
Mystic Ami's statue.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.033
Okay, I think I'm
starting to understand

00:06:37.116 --> 00:06:39.616
everything here.
Just one problem.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.825
That's not where the
statue was last time.

00:06:41.908 --> 00:06:43.200
[ANDREWS]
Um... Yes.

00:06:43.283 --> 00:06:44.408
You're right.

00:06:44.491 --> 00:06:46.366
You did seem
surprised back then.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.325
But what is
she doing over there?

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:49.700
Oh, no.

00:06:49.783 --> 00:06:51.116
Woah.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.450
Does that mean someone
moved it without you knowing?

00:06:53.533 --> 00:06:55.825
[PHOENIX] If I'm right, the
statue was only delivered here

00:06:55.908 --> 00:06:57.783
a day before the theft.

00:06:57.866 --> 00:07:00.450
The detective guarding
the warehouse, Luke Atmey,

00:07:00.533 --> 00:07:01.950
is the only one who
could've moved it.

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:04.366
[LUKE chuckles]

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.575
[PHOENIX]
The question is why he moved it.

00:07:06.658 --> 00:07:08.950
Furthermore, does
this have anything to do

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:11.200
with our new case?

00:07:11.283 --> 00:07:14.450
Again. Sorry.
I sincerely apologize.

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:15.866
[MAYA]
Don't worry about it!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.741
The urn looks the way
it's supposed to now.

00:07:17.825 --> 00:07:19.658
If anything, we should
be thanking you!

00:07:19.741 --> 00:07:21.658
Oh. Really? That's great!

00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.491
[MAYA laughs]

00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:34.033
I'm the new boss around here!
Watcha gonna do about it?

00:07:34.116 --> 00:07:35.783
Hey. New guy.

00:07:35.866 --> 00:07:37.575
Bring me a cup a joe,
will yah? Pronto.

00:07:37.658 --> 00:07:39.241
[PHOENIX groans]

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.783
Just so you know,

00:07:40.866 --> 00:07:42.950
that's where the victim was
sitting seconds before he died.

00:07:43.033 --> 00:07:45.366
[screams]

00:07:47.825 --> 00:07:50.450
[GUMSHOE] Man, today's
been a real train wreck

00:07:50.533 --> 00:07:51.450
for you guys, huh?

00:07:51.533 --> 00:07:53.200
I guess.

00:07:53.283 --> 00:07:54.783
You got that right!

00:07:54.866 --> 00:07:59.366
That caffeine-obsessed cyclops
made us look like total idiots!

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.575
That's a rough one.
I feel for you two.

00:08:01.658 --> 00:08:03.950
Wait, what?
That's not like you at all.

00:08:04.033 --> 00:08:06.075
Usually you're like,
"Serves you right!

00:08:06.158 --> 00:08:08.866
You got what you deserved!"
[laughs]

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.741
Or something along those lines.

00:08:10.825 --> 00:08:12.491
Well, I can tell when
someone puts their heart

00:08:12.575 --> 00:08:15.491
into their work, like
you did, so... You know?

00:08:15.575 --> 00:08:17.700
That, and I can sympathize
when things don't work out

00:08:17.783 --> 00:08:19.616
for hardworking people.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.575
Things rarely go the way
I want in my line of work.

00:08:22.658 --> 00:08:25.408
Wow, Dick, you're so thoughtful.
That's a shock.

00:08:25.491 --> 00:08:26.950
Oh. Oh!

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.575
While you're feeling talky,
what happened to Mask DeMasque

00:08:28.658 --> 00:08:29.783
after the trial?

00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:32.491
Him? That detective
that played dress-up?

00:08:32.575 --> 00:08:35.533
Serves him right!
The guy got what he deserved!

00:08:35.616 --> 00:08:37.283
[laughs

00:08:37.366 --> 00:08:39.741
Now there's the
Gumshoe we know and love.

00:08:39.825 --> 00:08:42.325
At least we know
there's nothing wrong with him.

00:08:42.408 --> 00:08:43.825
--By the way...
--[GUMSHOE] Huh?

00:08:43.908 --> 00:08:45.491
Would you mind telling us
a little bit about the victim

00:08:45.575 --> 00:08:47.325
who died here the other night?

00:08:47.408 --> 00:08:49.241
[GUMSHOE]
Sure thing, pal.

00:08:49.325 --> 00:08:52.450
Kane Bullard, the CEO of
KB Security and a big fella

00:08:52.533 --> 00:08:53.991
in his own right.

00:08:54.075 --> 00:08:56.575
His corpse was
found at 9 this morning.

00:08:56.658 --> 00:09:00.491
However, his estimated time
of death is 1 AM on the 12th.

00:09:00.575 --> 00:09:02.991
It really did happen at the
same time that Mask DeMasque

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.908
stole the urn, huh?

00:09:04.991 --> 00:09:06.783
Why did it take
an entire day for someone

00:09:06.866 --> 00:09:08.116
to discover the body?

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.991
[GUMSHOE] Well, his corpse
was stashed away inside

00:09:10.075 --> 00:09:12.783
that big safe,
if you can believe it.

00:09:12.866 --> 00:09:14.075
Nobody had heard from him,

00:09:14.158 --> 00:09:16.366
and when they opened
the safe in the morning...

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.116
[PHOENIX]
Out fell the body.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.283
[gasps]

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.700
[GUMSHOE] Also, it seems
like this guy was involved

00:09:22.783 --> 00:09:25.533
in some shady
business practices.

00:09:25.616 --> 00:09:26.783
Shady like how?

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:29.075
If a company hired his
firm, they'd spy on 'em,

00:09:29.158 --> 00:09:31.908
learn their secrets, then
sell the information to rivals.

00:09:31.991 --> 00:09:34.575
Wow. Sounds like
a grade-A crook.

00:09:34.658 --> 00:09:36.491
[GUMSHOE] The firm was
even in charge of security

00:09:36.575 --> 00:09:38.450
for someone robbed
by Mask DeMasque.

00:09:38.533 --> 00:09:41.200
But they screwed it up
and lost the victim's trust.

00:09:41.283 --> 00:09:42.200
That's interesting.

00:09:42.283 --> 00:09:44.075
--[thud]
--[BOTH gasp]

00:09:44.158 --> 00:09:45.116
[PHOENIX]
What are you doing?

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.575
I'm tryin' to
open this dumb safe!

00:09:46.658 --> 00:09:48.075
What's it look like?

00:09:48.158 --> 00:09:51.158
[PHOENIX] I... don't think you
understand how safes work.

00:09:51.241 --> 00:09:53.325
[GUMSHOE] It's worth noting
somebody must've opened that

00:09:53.408 --> 00:09:54.658
on the night of the crime.

00:09:54.741 --> 00:09:57.866
After all, the victim's body
was hidden in there.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.991
Also... According
to company records,

00:10:00.075 --> 00:10:02.658
Ron DeLite had the
clearance needed to open it.

00:10:02.741 --> 00:10:04.491
But there are plenty
of others with the same level

00:10:04.575 --> 00:10:06.366
of access as him, aren't there?

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.450
[GUMSHOE]
Of course there are, but still--

00:10:08.533 --> 00:10:10.491
[alarm blares]

00:10:10.575 --> 00:10:12.408
[PHOENIX]
Maya?!

00:10:12.491 --> 00:10:14.950
Sorry! I wanted to see
what the button was for.

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:16.408
[GUMSHOE]
It's an emergency buzzer!

00:10:16.491 --> 00:10:18.575
Can't you read?
It says right there!

00:10:18.658 --> 00:10:20.283
Oops. Shoulda looked.

00:10:20.366 --> 00:10:22.450
[GUMSHOE] It sets off an alarm
in the basement guard room

00:10:22.533 --> 00:10:24.616
that tells security
to high-tail it here.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.866
I have to wonder.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:27.950
The other night,
was that button pressed?

00:10:28.033 --> 00:10:30.450
[GUMSHOE] I had the same
thought, so I asked around.

00:10:30.533 --> 00:10:33.158
Security says there's no
record of the alarm sounding.

00:10:33.241 --> 00:10:34.741
Plus, we dusted
the button for prints

00:10:34.825 --> 00:10:36.241
and didn't find a thing.

00:10:36.325 --> 00:10:38.116
[PHOENIX] I'm surprised
the buzzer wasn't used.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.658
[BUTZ] You again?
You need somethin' big man?

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:42.741
Larry!

00:10:42.825 --> 00:10:44.408
[MAYA giggles]

00:10:44.491 --> 00:10:45.575
[chuckles]

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.116
I am so jealous!

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.158
And here I was workin' my butt
off while you're out there

00:10:55.241 --> 00:10:56.491
livin' the dream!

00:10:56.575 --> 00:10:58.450
--[PHOENIX gasps]
--[BUTZ] It's a weekday, man!

00:10:58.533 --> 00:11:00.325
And you two are on
an afternoon date?

00:11:00.408 --> 00:11:02.491
Oh, no. It's nothing
like that at all.

00:11:02.575 --> 00:11:05.033
We're just here to investigate
CEO Bullard's death.

00:11:05.116 --> 00:11:06.450
Oh. Yeah.

00:11:06.533 --> 00:11:08.950
That's right, that
guy died. Didn't he?

00:11:09.033 --> 00:11:10.366
C'mon.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.491
[MAYA] All right, let's actually
get down to business.

00:11:12.575 --> 00:11:14.700
Larry, were you here on
the night of the murder?

00:11:14.783 --> 00:11:17.908
Huh? Yeah, of course I was.

00:11:17.991 --> 00:11:19.991
[PHOENIX] That's a lie
if I ever heard one.

00:11:20.075 --> 00:11:23.366
What? No! I was here!
Why wouldn't I be?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.866
[PHOENIX]
Yeah, you were playing hooky.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.991
Whaddya mean? I resent that!

00:11:27.075 --> 00:11:29.366
Besides. Do you have
proof I left my post?

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:31.033
Because I don't think you do!

00:11:31.116 --> 00:11:32.908
[PHOENIX] I thought
you found Ron's wallet.

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:35.491
At least, that's what
you testified at the trial.

00:11:35.575 --> 00:11:38.200
[BUTZ] Oh, yeah.
It was just two days ago.

00:11:38.283 --> 00:11:40.491
I saw it on the ground outside
my building at work.

00:11:40.575 --> 00:11:42.366
It's clear.
If you found it outside

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:44.991
two nights ago, you
must've snuck out of work!

00:11:45.075 --> 00:11:49.033
[yells]

00:11:49.116 --> 00:11:52.658
[BUTZ] You're not sayin'
it's my fault, are ya?

00:11:52.741 --> 00:11:54.616
It's not my fault
he's dead, right?

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.533
[PHOENIX] Did you bail
for the usual reason?

00:11:56.616 --> 00:11:58.158
Usual reason?

00:11:58.241 --> 00:12:00.283
If you're insinuating that
I left to meet a girl

00:12:00.366 --> 00:12:01.408
then you're way off!

00:12:01.491 --> 00:12:02.991
[PHOENIX]
I knew it.

00:12:03.075 --> 00:12:08.575
[BUTZ wails] I'm a fool.
If I was here, he'd be alive!

00:12:08.658 --> 00:12:10.200
[MAYA]
Oh, Larry.

00:12:10.283 --> 00:12:12.491
[BUTZ whimpers]

00:12:12.575 --> 00:12:16.075
Huh? Ah! How can I ever
make up for what I've done?

00:12:16.158 --> 00:12:17.950
I must atone, Nick!

00:12:18.033 --> 00:12:20.741
[PHOENIX] Well, for starters,
you better tell me this...

00:12:20.825 --> 00:12:23.658
Did the buzzer really
not go off that night?

00:12:23.741 --> 00:12:25.866
I had the same thought,
so I asked around.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.408
Security says there's no record
of the alarm sounding.

00:12:28.491 --> 00:12:30.450
Nope! Had to check before.

00:12:30.533 --> 00:12:32.866
No logs of it
goin' off all night.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.491
[MAYA] Would you mind
looking one more time?

00:12:34.575 --> 00:12:35.908
Just in case?

00:12:35.991 --> 00:12:40.200
[BUTZ] Fine. I can't
say no to you, Maya. Let's see.

00:12:40.283 --> 00:12:42.700
Well, I figured.
We might as well try.

00:12:42.783 --> 00:12:44.033
Yeah, but I doubt it'll help.

00:12:44.116 --> 00:12:45.908
Not even Larry could make
that kind of mistake.

00:12:45.991 --> 00:12:47.033
[BUTZ]
Aww, crap!

00:12:47.116 --> 00:12:48.241
[BOTH gasp]

00:12:48.325 --> 00:12:51.658
[BUTZ whimpers]
I made a mistake.

00:12:51.741 --> 00:12:52.825
[MAYA, PHOENIX gasp]

00:12:52.908 --> 00:12:54.991
I don't know how!

00:12:55.075 --> 00:12:59.575
It says it went off during
the night around 1 AM or so.

00:12:59.658 --> 00:13:02.033
Around 1 AM?

00:13:02.116 --> 00:13:04.575
That lines up perfectly with
the time of the murder!

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:08.616
[BUTZ sobs]
Say it ain't so!

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.075
I can't believe I missed that!

00:13:11.158 --> 00:13:13.491
[PHOENIX] Yeah, I can't
believe it either, buddy.

00:13:13.575 --> 00:13:16.533
Let's go ask Ron for some
clarification on that night.

00:13:16.616 --> 00:13:17.658
[MAYA]
Hmm.

00:13:21.491 --> 00:13:23.283
I'm begging you Mister Wright.

00:13:23.366 --> 00:13:26.825
Begging! Please!
Don't abandon me!

00:13:26.908 --> 00:13:28.200
Ron, if you want my help,

00:13:28.283 --> 00:13:30.033
you're going to have to
start telling me the truth.

00:13:30.116 --> 00:13:31.491
Do I have your word?

00:13:31.575 --> 00:13:33.116
Yeah.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.366
All right. Now tell me where you
were the night of the murder.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.200
And I mean where
you really were.

00:13:37.283 --> 00:13:38.616
Okay...

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:40.866
At 1 AM on September the 12th.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:44.658
You weren't at Lordly Tailor,
but at K-B Security, right?

00:13:46.825 --> 00:13:47.950
[RON]
Since I used to work there,

00:13:48.033 --> 00:13:49.991
I knew where the
CEO's office was.

00:13:50.075 --> 00:13:51.950
I knocked, but there
was no answer.

00:13:52.033 --> 00:13:54.491
[RON] So I used the key card
to unlock the door.

00:13:54.575 --> 00:13:56.158
I didn't notice,
but when I went inside,

00:13:56.241 --> 00:13:57.991
someone was there in the dark.

00:13:58.075 --> 00:14:01.325
[RON] Then suddenly they bashed
me over the head with something!

00:14:01.408 --> 00:14:02.866
[MAYA] Could you tell
if it was the C.E.O

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.158
when you looked at him?

00:14:04.241 --> 00:14:06.658
[RON]
No. Whoever it was ran away

00:14:06.741 --> 00:14:09.491
while I was stunned, so I didn't
see what they looked like.

00:14:09.575 --> 00:14:12.700
[RON] But when I came to, I saw
Mr. Bullard dead on the ground!

00:14:12.783 --> 00:14:15.616
[RON] I thought I had to do
something about the body.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.200
[MAYA]
And what did you do after that?

00:14:18.283 --> 00:14:20.283
[RON] What do you think?
I got out of there!

00:14:20.366 --> 00:14:21.908
Sure, I hid the body
in the safe,

00:14:21.991 --> 00:14:24.033
but that's 'cause I was
afraid of how it'd look.

00:14:24.116 --> 00:14:26.866
See? That's all I did, I swear!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.075
[PHOENIX sighs]

00:14:28.158 --> 00:14:30.283
I was scared the
police would find out, so...

00:14:30.366 --> 00:14:31.950
I turned myself in.

00:14:32.033 --> 00:14:33.866
If I had been found
guilty as Mask DeMasque

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.616
in the previous trial, then that
could have been my alibi.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.283
One more thing.

00:14:38.366 --> 00:14:41.116
Can you recall when you
received this blackmail letter?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:43.366
Let's see...
When was it, again?

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.491
It's kinda hard to
tell them all apart.

00:14:45.575 --> 00:14:47.283
There've been so many.

00:14:47.366 --> 00:14:49.908
What does that mean?
This isn't the first one?

00:14:49.991 --> 00:14:52.616
No. But this is the first
one that ever called me out

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.158
to a specific location,
if that counts for anything.

00:14:55.241 --> 00:14:56.241
Do you at least
remember when

00:14:56.325 --> 00:14:57.825
you received the first one?

00:14:57.908 --> 00:14:59.366
I could never forget that.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:01.866
I got the first letter only a
few days after my debut

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.325
as Mask DeMasque.

00:15:03.408 --> 00:15:04.866
Ron, you said
you'd tell the truth.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.575
You aren't the phantom thief!

00:15:06.658 --> 00:15:08.866
It was Ace Detective Luke Atmey.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.283
No, it wasn't!

00:15:11.366 --> 00:15:13.866
I know it looks like I'm lying
because it wasn't me who broke

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.616
into Lordly Tailor that night.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:19.783
But still! It really was me
on all the other heists!

00:15:19.866 --> 00:15:20.783
[gasps]

00:15:20.866 --> 00:15:22.283
I'm not lying.

00:15:22.366 --> 00:15:25.200
Someone apparently spotted me
on my inaugural adventure.

00:15:25.283 --> 00:15:27.991
I know because it said
so in the first blackmail.

00:15:28.075 --> 00:15:29.991
Something like
"I know you did it."

00:15:30.075 --> 00:15:32.283
You got busted
on your first theft?

00:15:32.366 --> 00:15:33.783
And from then on,

00:15:33.866 --> 00:15:36.408
I started receiving plans
and instructions in the mail.

00:15:36.491 --> 00:15:38.200
[PHOENIX]
Plans?

00:15:38.283 --> 00:15:40.866
[RON] They'd tell me what
to steal and how to do it.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:43.658
They detailed security
blind spots, escape routes,

00:15:43.741 --> 00:15:45.533
and even training methods.

00:15:45.616 --> 00:15:47.408
Are you telling me
your heists were all planned

00:15:47.491 --> 00:15:48.825
by someone else?

00:15:48.908 --> 00:15:50.325
Yes. After the first one,

00:15:50.408 --> 00:15:52.616
I was simply carrying out
my mysterious orders.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.700
If I didn't, they'd tell
the cops! Pretty cool, huh?

00:15:55.783 --> 00:15:59.450
Why is he so happy
about being exploited?

00:15:59.533 --> 00:16:01.991
[PHOENIX] So Ron was
Mask DeMasque after all.

00:16:02.075 --> 00:16:04.033
But someone else
is behind the thefts.

00:16:04.116 --> 00:16:06.658
Someone who planned
it all out in detail.

00:16:06.741 --> 00:16:08.616
[RON] All I had to do was
put the treasures I stole

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.616
into the designated
safe-deposit box.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.283
Then just sit back
and wait for the cash

00:16:13.366 --> 00:16:14.908
to arrive in the mail.

00:16:14.991 --> 00:16:17.033
[PHOENIX]
You even got a reward out of it?

00:16:17.116 --> 00:16:19.450
[MAYA] Is that why you went
after the Kurain urn, then?

00:16:19.533 --> 00:16:22.450
I didn't. I've never
even seen that urn.

00:16:22.533 --> 00:16:24.075
All I do is steal
what I'm told to,

00:16:24.158 --> 00:16:26.325
and that urn wasn't
in my instructions.

00:16:26.408 --> 00:16:29.575
Ron, do you swear everything
you've just said is the truth?

00:16:29.658 --> 00:16:32.075
Yes. And now that
it's out, I'm done for.

00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:33.700
If there's one thing
Dessie won't stomach,

00:16:33.783 --> 00:16:35.241
it's breaking the law.

00:16:35.325 --> 00:16:37.991
When she finds out,
she's never gonna forgive me.

00:16:38.075 --> 00:16:40.408
If you knew that,
why'd you become a thief?

00:16:40.491 --> 00:16:41.533
I had to!

00:16:41.616 --> 00:16:44.033
She spends money
like it grows on trees!

00:16:44.116 --> 00:16:47.075
You see, I love her,
compulsive spending and all,

00:16:47.158 --> 00:16:50.033
but there's no job that could
bring in enough money for her!

00:16:50.116 --> 00:16:52.533
Except being a thief, I figured.

00:16:52.616 --> 00:16:53.991
[BOTH chuckle]

00:16:54.075 --> 00:16:55.950
I tried telling her
I was Mask DeMasque,

00:16:56.033 --> 00:16:58.450
but she immediately
laughed at the idea!

00:16:58.533 --> 00:17:00.158
She thought I was joking around!

00:17:00.241 --> 00:17:02.616
To be fair, I don't think
I would have believed it either.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.325
Can't blame her.

00:17:04.408 --> 00:17:07.533
[RON] Anyway, I wanted
to tell you something.

00:17:07.616 --> 00:17:09.241
I heard that detective
who's taking credit

00:17:09.325 --> 00:17:12.075
for my thievery is having his
trial at the exact same time

00:17:12.158 --> 00:17:14.491
as mine, in the
courtroom next door!

00:17:14.575 --> 00:17:15.908
Well, that's surprising.

00:17:15.991 --> 00:17:18.450
Hold on. But we know that wacky
wordsmith isn't actually

00:17:18.533 --> 00:17:20.033
Mask DeMasque, don't we?

00:17:20.116 --> 00:17:22.450
[RON]
Right, he's not. I am!

00:17:22.533 --> 00:17:23.741
[PHOENIX] It doesn't
matter what we know

00:17:23.825 --> 00:17:26.283
if he's claiming to be guilty.

00:17:26.366 --> 00:17:28.325
I have one more question
that I have to ask you

00:17:28.408 --> 00:17:29.658
before we're finished.

00:17:29.741 --> 00:17:30.950
Of course, ask away.

00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:33.158
Be completely honest
in your response.

00:17:33.241 --> 00:17:34.700
Did you kill Kane Bullard?

00:17:34.783 --> 00:17:36.908
No, I didn't! Please.

00:17:36.991 --> 00:17:38.283
Please believe me!

00:17:38.366 --> 00:17:39.491
[MAYA grunts]

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.116
I'm sorry.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.616
As you can imagine, I was
just trying to help my Ronnie.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.950
Kinda backfired
on you there, didn't it?

00:17:51.033 --> 00:17:52.741
[PHOENIX]
Don't say that.

00:17:52.825 --> 00:17:55.783
Nicky boy, please.
We really need your help.

00:17:55.866 --> 00:17:58.533
Ronnie's not a killer, I know
him better than anyone!

00:17:58.616 --> 00:18:00.075
I'm on your side.

00:18:00.158 --> 00:18:01.825
[sighs]
Thank you so much!

00:18:01.908 --> 00:18:03.200
I just don't know what
to do anymore.

00:18:03.283 --> 00:18:05.241
I feel so useless.

00:18:05.325 --> 00:18:07.950
And that detective!
He's infuriating!

00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:10.450
I want to knock that pointy
nose off his stupid face!

00:18:10.533 --> 00:18:12.158
Knowing that, I'm less
surprised that you barged

00:18:12.241 --> 00:18:15.033
into his office, but you still
shouldn't have done that.

00:18:15.116 --> 00:18:16.658
[DESIRÉE]
I had to do something!

00:18:16.741 --> 00:18:18.866
Ronnie was in major trouble!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.991
We talked to him earlier,
and despite everything,

00:18:21.075 --> 00:18:23.700
he's still claiming to
be Mask DeMasque.

00:18:23.783 --> 00:18:25.325
[DESIRÉE]
He's so silly.

00:18:25.408 --> 00:18:28.200
I know everything there is to
know about that cinnamon roll.

00:18:28.283 --> 00:18:30.158
He always looks before he leaps.

00:18:30.241 --> 00:18:32.616
Most of the time,
he looks and doesn't leap.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.908
He's so fainthearted!

00:18:33.991 --> 00:18:36.408
He just doesn't have it
in him to be a thief.

00:18:36.491 --> 00:18:38.491
Right. You know him the best.

00:18:38.575 --> 00:18:40.241
[PHOENIX]
I guess opposites attract.

00:18:40.325 --> 00:18:41.533
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:18:41.616 --> 00:18:43.116
Oh. Just thinking
out loud about how these two

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.408
are so different, yet somehow
ended up married to each other.

00:18:46.491 --> 00:18:47.700
Come on, now.

00:18:47.783 --> 00:18:49.866
You don't have to
sound so perplexed.

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.491
It was love at first sight.

00:18:51.575 --> 00:18:52.950
For me, at least.

00:18:53.033 --> 00:18:54.825
Wow! That's a surprise!

00:18:54.908 --> 00:18:56.491
[DESIRÉE] It wouldn't be
if you'd been there.

00:18:56.575 --> 00:18:58.033
Ronnie saved my life.

00:18:59.033 --> 00:19:00.575
Back then,
I was working in a bank.

00:19:00.658 --> 00:19:03.366
And one day, two men
suddenly rushed in to rob us.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.991
[DESIRÉE] I can't stand
people like that, so naturally,

00:19:08.075 --> 00:19:10.283
I gave 'em a piece of my mind!

00:19:10.366 --> 00:19:12.700
[PHOENIX] You talked down
to armed robbers?

00:19:12.783 --> 00:19:15.075
[DESIRÉE]
Yeah, and they took me hostage.

00:19:15.158 --> 00:19:17.658
I was so scared.

00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:20.658
But then help arrived--
in the form of Ronnie.

00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:24.825
Stop! You thugs leave her alone!

00:19:24.908 --> 00:19:27.075
[DESIRÉE] Crying and
swinging his arms like crazy,

00:19:27.158 --> 00:19:29.491
he attacked the two robbers.

00:19:29.575 --> 00:19:32.533
I think...
that's when I realized.

00:19:32.616 --> 00:19:34.950
He's the kind of guy
who has real courage.

00:19:35.033 --> 00:19:38.408
The courage to risk his life
when it matters most.

00:19:38.491 --> 00:19:39.950
My Ronnie.

00:19:43.408 --> 00:19:45.575
Tomorrow, let's send
that Prosecutor Godot

00:19:45.658 --> 00:19:48.116
from espresso to depresso!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.575
--Get it?
--[PEARL] Mystic Maya, Mr. Nick!

00:19:50.658 --> 00:19:52.533
Hey, you two!

00:19:52.616 --> 00:19:54.783
[MAYA]
Pearls!

00:19:54.866 --> 00:19:57.158
[PEARL]
It's the real deal, apparently!

00:19:57.241 --> 00:19:59.950
[MAYA gasps]
That's such great news!

00:20:00.033 --> 00:20:01.991
Thanks again. You rock!

00:20:02.075 --> 00:20:05.825
[PHOENIX] The urn. This
whole mess started with it.

00:20:05.908 --> 00:20:07.908
At 1 AM on the night
it was stolen,

00:20:07.991 --> 00:20:10.200
Ron was at K-B Security.

00:20:11.241 --> 00:20:12.491
[gasps]

00:20:12.575 --> 00:20:14.658
At the same time,
there was another Mask DeMasque

00:20:14.741 --> 00:20:17.741
in the Lordly Tailor
basement warehouse.

00:20:17.825 --> 00:20:20.741
Why'd Luke Atmey show up
there dressed like that?

00:20:20.825 --> 00:20:24.783
And why would he pick that time
in particular to steal the urn?

00:20:24.866 --> 00:20:27.366
Not to mention, why
was the statue moved?

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:30.700
There had to have been a reason.

00:20:30.783 --> 00:20:32.741
And that's not
all we don't know.

00:20:32.825 --> 00:20:36.908
Who attacked Ron in the
CEO's office at K-B Security?

00:20:36.991 --> 00:20:38.950
And that emergency buzzer.

00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:41.866
Why would the killer
let it be pressed?

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:45.450
He should've realized
security would rush there.

00:20:45.533 --> 00:20:47.950
Wait, did he do it
because he knew

00:20:48.033 --> 00:20:53.033
security would come?
Why didn't I see it before?

00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:56.241
[LUKE laughs]

00:20:59.325 --> 00:21:00.658
[PEARL]
I know that look!

00:21:00.741 --> 00:21:03.033
You just figured something
out, didn't you?

00:21:03.116 --> 00:21:05.866
Tomorrow's trial will
be a race against the clock.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:09.116
Aww. I was hoping we could
take this one nice and easy.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.616
Unfortunately, we can't.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.283
That won't cut it tomorrow.

00:21:22.783 --> 00:21:25.075
This court is hereby
in session for the trial

00:21:25.158 --> 00:21:26.658
of Ron DeLite.

00:21:26.741 --> 00:21:30.325
[PHOENIX] In a nearby courtroom,
another trial is set to begin.

00:21:34.991 --> 00:21:36.783
Court is now in
session for the trial

00:21:36.866 --> 00:21:39.450
of Luke Atmey.
Please take your seats.

00:21:39.533 --> 00:21:42.658
Two simultaneous
trials, linked at the core.

00:21:42.741 --> 00:21:46.533
I have to find the truth
and drag him to the stand...

00:21:46.616 --> 00:21:48.700
...before the verdict
is handed down!

00:23:20.991 --> 00:23:22.825
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.908 --> 00:23:24.950
The two tangled trials begin.

00:23:25.033 --> 00:23:27.408
In order to prove Ron's
innocence, I'll need to unveil

00:23:27.491 --> 00:23:30.450
the crimes of Detective Atmey,
who stands as the accused

00:23:30.533 --> 00:23:32.033
in the other ongoing trial.

00:23:32.116 --> 00:23:34.741
Which means it's
a battle against time!

00:23:34.825 --> 00:23:37.491
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:37.575 --> 00:23:40.616
Next episode: "The Stolen
Turnabout--Last Trial"!

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:41.825
Take that!

00:23:41.908 --> 00:23:43.616
[RON]
Please believe me!

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:47.491
[BUTZ]
Oh, come on, Nick! [wails]
